Title: Midnight Harbour
Credit: Written by
Author: Scene Reader Studio Technologies LLC
Draft date: July 2026

FADE IN:

EXT. HARBOUR DOCKS - DAWN

Fog clings to the water. A BODY floats face-down near the pier.

DETECTIVE SARAH MARSH (40s, weathered) crouches at the edge. Rookie OFFICER DANNY COLE (late 20s) hangs back.

MARSH
How long has he been in the water?

COLE
ME says six hours. Maybe more.

MARSH
He didn't fall. Look at the entry angle.

INT. POLICE PRECINCT - BRIEFING ROOM - DAY

Maps and photos cover every surface. CAPTAIN HOLT (60s) addresses a room of detectives.

HOLT
Three bodies in six weeks. Same harbour. Same method.

MARSH
Or cleaning house.

EXT. HARBOUR MASTER'S OFFICE - DAY

A converted shipping container. Marsh knocks. HARBOUR MASTER JENKINS (70s) opens the door.

JENKINS
I already told the other detectives everything I know.

MARSH
Tell me again.

INT. HARBOUR MASTER'S OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

Charts and tide tables everywhere. Jenkins pours coffee without asking.

JENKINS
The Meridian came in at 0300. She wasn't on the schedule.

MARSH
Who owns her?

JENKINS
Registered to a shell company. Three layers deep.

EXT. MERIDIAN - CARGO SHIP - DAY

Marsh and Cole approach the vessel. TWO GUARDS block the gangway.

MARSH
Detective Marsh. Questions about your cargo manifest.

GUARD #1
You'll need to talk to our legal team.

INT. MERIDIAN - CARGO HOLD - DAY

Dark. Massive. Marsh moves her flashlight across stacked containers.

COLE
What are we looking for?

MARSH
We'll know it when we find it.

EXT. HARBOUR DOCKS - NIGHT

Rain. Marsh stands alone at the water's edge.

MARSH
There's a fourth.

INT. FORENSICS LAB - NIGHT

DR. ELENA VASQUEZ (30s) shows Marsh photographs.

VASQUEZ
Same ligature marks. Same timeline. Ten years. Maybe more.

INT. WATERFRONT WAREHOUSE - CONTINUOUS

Empty shelves. Salt and rust.

MARSH
Police! Don't move!

A FIGURE bolts for the back exit.

INT. POLICE PRECINCT - MARSH'S DESK - NIGHT

Marsh spreads everything out. Photographs. Manifests. Tide tables.

MARSH
You've been here the whole time.

EXT. HARBOUR DOCKS - PRE-DAWN

Fog again. Marsh finds a button caught in a piling. Distinctive. Expensive.

MARSH
Got you.

INT. POLICE PRECINCT - CAPTAIN'S OFFICE - DAY

Marsh drops a file on Holt's desk.

MARSH
The Meridian is the distraction. The real operation has been running out of the harbour master's office for three years.

HOLT
Jenkins?

MARSH
Jenkins.

EXT. HARBOUR MASTER'S OFFICE - DAY

Jenkins emerges in handcuffs.

JENKINS
You're better than I thought.

MARSH
I know.

COLE
How did you know it was him?

MARSH
He poured the coffee before I told him why I was there. That's never it. But it's where I started.

She turns back to the harbour.

MARSH (CONT'D)
Four bodies. One button. A ship that wasn't supposed to be here. Some things you can't hide in the fog.

FADE OUT.

THE END
